Let me look at the `remove_vc_all_except` function more carefully. The issue is that when `FLAC__metadata_object_vorbiscomment_delete_comment(block, i)` is called, it resizes the comments array. If the array is reallocated to a smaller size, the old memory is freed. But the loop in `remove_vc_all_except` accesses `block->data.vorbis_comment.comments[i]` in the condition check. Let me trace through this:

In `remove_vc_all_except`:
```c
for(i = 0; i < block->data.vorbis_comment.num_comments; ) {
    int field_name_found = false;
    for(j = 0; j < num_field_names; j++) {
        const uint32_t length = (j == (num_field_names - 1))?(uint32_t)strlen(field_names[j]):(uint32_t)(strchr(field_names[j],'=')-field_names[j]);
        if(FLAC__metadata_object_vorbiscomment_entry_matches(block->data.vorbis_comment.comments[i], field_names[j], length)) {
            field_name_found = true;
            break;
        }
    }
    if(!field_name_found) {
        FLAC__metadata_object_vorbiscomment_delete_comment(block, i);
        *needs_write = true;
    }
    else
        i++;
}
```

When `FLAC__metadata_object_vorbiscomment_delete_comment(block, i)` is called, it calls `resize_comments` which may realloc the `comments` array. If the realloc moves the memory, the old pointer is freed. But the loop re-reads `block->data.vorbis_comment.comments[i]` each iteration, so that should be fine.

